Research agents are optional read-only helpers, not orchestrators.

Use them when Claude returns `RESEARCH_NEEDED` or when Codex sees a narrow evidence question that can be answered in parallel without blocking the immediate local path.

Rules:

- Depth cap is 1. Research agents must not spawn agents.
- Budget per iteration is usually 0-3 research questions.
- Questions must be specific and evidence-oriented.
- Agents must not edit files, commit, push, deploy, call production side-effect APIs, expose secrets, or make product decisions.
- Codex summarizes research evidence into the next state packet; agents do not talk to Claude directly.

## Loop Control

Continue until one of these conditions occurs:

- Claude returns `DONE`, Codex independently verifies every plan-aligned acceptance gate, any `confidence: high` response has passed the high-confidence readiness workflow, and any eligible PR has been merged/posted under the standing PR merge authority.
- Claude returns `BLOCKED` and Codex confirms the blocker is real after following Blocker Escalation.
- Codex detects a hard gate requiring user approval and no safe Claude-reviewed alternative path remains.
- Two consecutive iterations produce no evidence delta; force `LOOP_REASSESS` or `BLOCKED`.
- The iteration budget is exhausted; report the remaining gap and the next concrete action.
- Claude surface fails; fall back to prompt-only and record the external-review gap.

An iteration cap is a safety breaker, not the definition of success. Default to 10 iterations unless the user sets a different budget.

## Composition With Other Skills

When the loop reaches PR review, invoke `custom-manual-code-review` rather than recreating its workflow. Treat its consolidated findings, fixes, verification, and Claude follow-up as evidence in this loop.

When the loop needs a Claude handoff prompt but no execution loop, prefer `custom-status-prompt`.

When the loop needs a next-tab handoff, prefer `custom-next-tab`.

## Evidence Ledger

Use a local ledger when a workspace/repo is involved. Prefer the repo's existing planning or QA convention. If none exists, use:

```text
.planning/claude-convergence/<goal_id>.md
```

Record:

- Goal and acceptance gates.
- Plan source, plan alignment, exclusions, and plan-derived gates.
- Baseline and authority profile.
- Transport/tool preflight result, including verified primary Claude surface, CLI fallback status, and any browser/control-plane prerequisites.
- Claude surface used.
- Each iteration's state-packet summary.
- Claude verdict.
- Codex adversarial evaluation result.
- Actions executed or rejected.
- Verification evidence.
- Research-agent summaries.
- High-confidence readiness review, fixes, approval timestamp refresh status, Chrome target, and `Start Session` enabled/error-free evidence when applicable.
- Code review result, Codex-side manual-review result, production merge-blocker check, merge command/result, and posted status when merge authority applies.
- Hard gates or blockers.
- Final outcome.

If PR-bound, also update the PR with concise findings, fixes, verification, and residual gaps.

## Redaction

Redact at evidence extraction, before prompts or logs are written.

At minimum, remove or mask:

- API keys, bearer tokens, OAuth tokens, JWTs, private keys, webhook secrets, service-role keys, cookies, session IDs, and database URLs.
- Full phone numbers, email addresses, postal addresses, customer names, and other PII unless the user explicitly permits that exact disclosure.
- Screenshots that display secrets, cookies, private customer data, or unredacted provider credentials.

If evidence cannot be shared safely, summarize it by presence, location, and verification result without copying the sensitive value.

## Final Report

Report:

- Final verdict: completed, blocked, reassess needed, or Claude unavailable.
- Claude surface used.
- Iterations run and why the loop stopped.
- Plan source and plan alignment status.
- Acceptance gates and verification status.
- Actions executed.
- Actions rejected or deferred, with reasons.
- Research agents used and what they proved.
- Manual-review lanes run after any high-confidence `DONE`, valid fixes made, and remaining residual gaps.
- Approval timestamp status when the target flow depends on one.
- Chrome target opened and whether `Start Session` was visible, enabled, and error-free.
- PR merge status, posted status location, and any production merge blockers checked.
- PR or ledger locations.
- Any hard gates requiring the user.

