docs/course-production/STYLE-BLOCK.md:1:Use a flat hand drawn sticker sheet illustration style on a bright cornflower blue background, with simple objects floating in active negative space rather than forming a realistic scene. Draw every shape with thick rounded black outlines, slightly uneven pressure, visible wobble, and imperfect curves; keep line weight bold and consistent. Use flat fills only: cornflower blue, sunflower yellow, golden yellow, tangerine orange, pale cream, warm white, black, small touches of peach skin tone and light gray hair. Characters are small, friendly, and simplified, with dot eyes, tiny noses, minimal mouths, round heads, chunky hair silhouettes, cylindrical arms and legs, oversized shoes, and squat proportions; identity comes from pose, hair, outfit color, and one clear prop. Detail is icon level: strong silhouettes, a few interior marks, no rendering. Add balanced doodles like puffy clouds, sparkle stars, speech bubbles with dots, music notes, hearts, grass tufts, motion ticks, signs, mugs, folders, keys, plants, and simple tools. Avoid realism, thin lines, gradients, shadows, perspective depth, texture, airbrush lighting, crowded scenes, tiny unreadable details, and polished vector perfection.
